---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SpecCard from '../components/SpecCard.astro';
import { isHeld } from '../data/publish-queue.js';

const held = isHeld('/oai-searchbot/');
---
<BaseLayout
  title="OAI-SearchBot: User-Agent, robots.txt Rules and How to Verify It | PromptDNS"
  description="OAI-SearchBot explained: what OpenAI's crawler does, its user-agent token, robots.txt behavior, how to verify it, and how to block or allow it."
  breadcrumb={[["Home", "/"], ["AI Web Infrastructure", "/ai-web-infrastructure/"], ["OAI-SearchBot"]]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/ai-web-infrastructure/" class="hover:text-accent">AI Web Infrastructure</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">OAI-SearchBot</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">OAI-SearchBot: User-Agent, robots.txt Rules and How to Verify It</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">OAI-SearchBot is OpenAI's crawler that indexes the web for ChatGPT Search. It honors robots.txt, and sites that block it do not appear in ChatGPT Search results. Its fetches resolve to OpenAI-hosted addresses, which is how you verify them.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="not-prose my-8" aria-label="Crawler specification" data-vs="speccard-wrap">
      <SpecCard
        name="OAI-SearchBot"
        operator="OpenAI"
        token="OAI-SearchBot"
        purpose="ChatGPT Search results"
        robots="honors Disallow: OAI-SearchBot"
        verify="Reverse DNS resolves to *.openai.com"
        evidence="Documented"
        verified="2026-10-28"
        href="/ai-crawlers-list/"
      />
    </section>

    <article class="rich-text mt-10 max-w-none">
      <h2>How to block OAI-SearchBot</h2>
      <p>Add this rule to your robots.txt at the root of your domain:</p>
      <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel-2 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-accent-soft">User-agent: OAI-SearchBot
Disallow: /</pre>
      <p>OAI-SearchBot is independent of GPTBot: blocking it removes you from ChatGPT Search while leaving training collection governed by the GPTBot rule.</p>

      <h2>How to allow OAI-SearchBot</h2>
      <p>If you want OAI-SearchBot to crawl your site, make sure no rule disallows it. An explicit allow looks like this:</p>
      <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel-2 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-accent-soft">User-agent: OAI-SearchBot
Allow: /</pre>
      <p>Then confirm from the live fetch with the <a href="/ai-crawler-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">AI crawler checker</a>, which reads your published robots.txt the way a crawler would.</p>

      <h2>How to verify OAI-SearchBot</h2>
      <p>The reliable check is reverse DNS on the fetching IP address. Run the lookup below against any visitor claiming the OAI-SearchBot token; a genuine fetch resolves inside OpenAI's address space, and a spoofed one does not.</p>
      <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel-2 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-accent-soft">dig +short -x <fetching-ip>
# A genuine OAI-SearchBot fetch resolves to an OpenAI address</pre>

      <aside class="mt-8 rounded-xl border-l-3 border-l-violet/50 bg-violet/5 p-5" aria-label="Practitioner field notes">
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-violet mb-2">Field notes</p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim italic">If citations in ChatGPT Search matter to you, OAI-SearchBot is the token to allow, and the one whose absence explains why a site never shows up in ChatGPT answers. It is also the cleanest example of why per-token rules matter: the same vendors run crawlers for search and training with completely different business implications.</p>
      </aside>

      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I appear in ChatGPT Search?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Allow OAI-SearchBot in robots.txt. Blocking it keeps your site out of ChatGPT Search results.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Is OAI-SearchBot the same as GPTBot?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No. GPTBot collects training data; OAI-SearchBot indexes for ChatGPT Search. They are separate crawlers with separate rules.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I verify OAI-SearchBot?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Reverse DNS on the fetching IP should resolve to an OpenAI address, same as GPTBot.</p></details>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        Related:
        <a href="/ai-crawlers-list/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">all AI crawlers</a>,
        <a href="/how-to-block-ai-crawlers/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">how to block AI crawlers</a>,
        <a href="/how-to-allow-ai-crawlers/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">how to allow AI crawlers</a>,
        <a href="/robots-txt-guide/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">robots.txt guide</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
